course: dictionary
lesson: 12791
title: Ejection: pushed out with force
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The noun ejection comes from the verb eject, which means to push or throw something out with force. When you meet a new word, read the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues.
explain: «The volcano gave a huge ejection of lava and ash into the sky.» Lava and ash are pushed out with force, so ejection means something being thrown out. Try your meaning in the sentence: "The volcano gave a huge throwing out of lava and ash" still makes sense.
explain: Ejection can also mean making someone leave a place. «The referee's ejection of the player ended his game early.» The clue is that the player had to stop playing and leave. Check it by swapping in "sending off": the sentence still works.
fact: Ejection is a noun, and its verb is eject.
fact: Ejection means pushing or throwing something out with force.
fact: Ejection can mean making someone leave a place, such as a sports player sent off.
fact: An ejection seat lets a pilot be shot out of a plane in an emergency.
fact: Ejection is used for lava and ash from a volcano, and for a disc or memory stick coming out of a computer.
exercise: «The volcano had a huge ejection of lava and ash.» What does ejection mean here? | *Being thrown out with great force | A type of rock that forms underground | Cooling slowly into soil | Being made to sit down quietly
exercise: «The referee gave the player an ejection from the game.» What happened to the player? | The player scored a goal | The player went to sleep on the bench | *The player was sent off and had to leave | The player was given a drink of water
exercise: An ejection seat is used in a plane. What does ejection seat mean? | *A seat that shoots a pilot out of a plane in an emergency | A seat with a soft cushion for passengers | A seat for resting during a long flight | A seat that folds up for landing
test: «Sam pressed eject, and the disc came out with a sharp ejection.» What did the computer do? | Played the disc faster | Broke the disc in two | *Pushed the disc out of the drive | Saved the disc onto the desktop
test: Which sentence uses ejection to mean making someone leave a place? | *The umpire's ejection of the coach ended the match for him | The lava had a huge ejection from the crater | The pilot pulled the ejection handle | The ash had a grey colour and a strong smell
exam: Ejection comes from a verb. Which verb is it? | erupt | project | *eject | inject
